1. Introduction

In production systems, applications need secrets such as:

database passwords
API keys
JWT secrets
OAuth tokens
Redis passwords

These secrets should NEVER be hardcoded inside:

Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
GitHub repository
source code

Instead, enterprises use:

AWS Secrets Manager
HashiCorp Vault
Kubernetes Secrets
Azure Key Vault

Most AWS-based production systems use:

AWS Secrets Manager.

2. Why Secrets Should Not Be Hardcoded

BAD EXAMPLE:

environment:
  DB_PASSWORD: mypassword123

Problems:

visible in GitHub
visible in docker inspect
difficult to rotate
insecure
violates enterprise security policies
